{
  "about": "The height of a line Chrome lays out at `line-height: normal`, one line of `Hxg` in a block, against `fontMetrics()` -- `Context2D::font_metrics` in Rust -- with each of its three values rounded and the three added. Read by tests/native_context2d.rs and tests/suite/text.test.js. `faces` names each face by the file under tests/assets/fonts it is made from and the bytes changed in it: `hheaLineGap`, `hhea`'s lineGap; `useTypoMetrics`, bit 7 of `OS/2`'s fsSelection; `typoLineGap`, `OS/2`'s sTypoLineGap. Amstelvar has 2000 units to the em, an `hhea` ascender and descender of 1900 and -500 and a typographic pair of 1500 and -500 with a gap of 400. A size is left out where its ascent, descent or gap in pixels is within 0.02 of a half: there CoreText's figure and FreeType's exact one can round apart.",
  "source": "HeadlessChrome/158.0.8127.18 (Chrome Headless Shell) on macOS, each face loaded as a FontFace from a data URL and checked with document.fonts.check, the line box read with getBoundingClientRect, measured 2026-11-11.",
  "faces": {
    "Amstelvar": {
      "from": "AmstelvarAlpha-VF.ttf"
    },
    "GapHhea": {
      "from": "AmstelvarAlpha-VF.ttf",
      "hheaLineGap": 200
    },
    "GapTypo": {
      "from": "AmstelvarAlpha-VF.ttf",
      "hheaLineGap": 200,
      "useTypoMetrics": true
    },
    "GapOdd": {
      "from": "AmstelvarAlpha-VF.ttf",
      "hheaLineGap": 67
    },
    "GapNegative": {
      "from": "AmstelvarAlpha-VF.ttf",
      "hheaLineGap": -200
    },
    "GapNegativeTypo": {
      "from": "AmstelvarAlpha-VF.ttf",
      "useTypoMetrics": true,
      "typoLineGap": -300,
      "hheaLineGap": 0
    },
    "Oswald": {
      "from": "Oswald/Oswald-VariableFont_wght.ttf"
    }
  },
